VERSION 0.4.1
  - Hot fix for regex pattern for links.

VERSION 0.4.0
  - Add parsing for links starting with http(s)://.


VERSION 0.3.0
  - Add parsing of nested loops. 
  - Improve parsing of special characters: >, <, >=, <=.
  - Add parsing of special words: LaTeX, TeX.
  - Add option --man, -m for applying conventions for man pages.
    Alpha feature. Not fully implemented.
  - Add option -M for emphasizing (monospace) text in the output.
  - Rewrite of the help text and man page.
  - Restructure the documentation and test folders.
  - doc/ contains the outputs of the help text through txt2man(1) and man.
  - test/ contains the outputs through txt2latex(1) and pdflatex(1).



VERSION 0.2.0
  - Improve parsing rules for handling verbatim blocks, special characters,
    inline math and math equations.
  - Fix quirks in handling blank lines in verbatim blocks.



VERSION 0.1.6
  - Handle inline math and special characters even if present in the same line.
  - Handle math equations $$...$$ i.e. treated as pure LaTeX.



VERSION 0.1.5
  -Add handling of math mode with underscore being a special character.



VERSION 0.1.4
  - Add automatically generated by txt2latex as a comment in the header.
  - Add paragraph on mathematics in the help text.


VERSION 0.1.3
  - Add option -P for adding custom packages or commands in the preambule.
  - Fix documentation glitches in the help text.
  - Add examples in the help text.



VERSION 0.1.2
  - Add protection of special characters $, % and & except in block display.



VERSION 0.1.1
  - Fix missing program name in help text.



VERSION 0.1
  Implementation of text pattern recognition based on txt2man:
    - sections
    - paragraphs
    - Description
    - Bullet lists
    - Enumerated lists
    - Literal display blocks

